      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first hotel on the site opened in 1766, a wooden building with 18 rooms, later becoming the Omni Homestead Resort.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.virginia.org/blog/post/homestead-warm-springs-pools/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Warm Springs Pools were expanded in the 1870s with a Ladies’ Bath House, allowing women to join restorative bathing.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.virginia.org/blog/post/homestead-warm-springs-pools/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area’s natural thermal springs have been used for recreation, medicine, and social reasons since 1761, giving the community its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dhr.virginia.gov/historic-registers/008-5025/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The district includes West Warm Springs, a historically African American community settled after the Civil War, many working in the resort industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dhr.virginia.gov/historic-registers/008-5025/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The water in these springs takes about twenty years to cycle through the Earth before resurfacing.",
